Let's say in your metaphysics you will be reincarnated somehow
in some sense anyway.

But do you want to have taken part in making it happen?  Or do
you just want your next deanimation to be a chance to have the
cards dealt again?  Why not just spend all your lives getting
reshuffled without ever getting down to playing?

A world view that says that nothing I do matters because I'm going
to both do it and not do it anyway...I find hard to think in.
So why bring up the topic?

On the other hand, if you really *don't* believe in automatic
metaphysical reincarnation, then it's crap, and there's nothing
"amusing" or "backward" about facing facts.

